# Docker build context hygiene.
#
# 🔴 This does NOT exist to save bytes — it exists so a `COPY` cannot pick up
# something that should never reach a registry. Both Dockerfiles COPY by NAME
# rather than `COPY . .`, and that is the real control; this is the second one.
#
# Keep `tests/`: both images deliberately COPY specific hermetic test files so a
# build can run them against the modules the image actually installed.

.git
.github
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# Local secrets and env files.
.env
.env.*

# Never COPYed, and no business being in a build context.
docs/
deploy/
*.md
LICENSE

# Build/run artefacts.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.log
